# Editorial rotation

The set decays by accretion, not by error. Reserve the tail of every session for a review of
**exactly one group**, taking the groups in turn; the next group due and any backlog are recorded in
`STATUS.md`. With no spare budget, say which group was due and carry it; never skip it silently.

| # | Group | Look especially for |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `docs/evidence.md` | a §2 row that no longer matches its §3; a result missing its P-point, domain or build |
| 2 | `docs/comparison.md`, `docs/problem.md` | restated evidence; a verdict cell whose qualification lives only in `evidence.md`; a requirement scored on since re-measured evidence |
| 3 | `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/control-plane.md` | design a measurement has overtaken; unimplemented design presented without its weight |
| 4 | `docs/economics.md`, `docs/glossary.md`, `lab/cost-model.md` | a modelled rate that lost its *hypothetical* label; a term defined twice |
| 5 | two `lab/test-*.md`, oldest reviewed first | a heading contradicted later in its file; a `Corrections` section grown into narrative; chronology; a rig whose flags the current build rejects |
| 6 | `lab/method-notes.md`, `lab/planned-experiments.md`, `lab/upstream-contributions.md`, `lab/README.md` | a rule told twice; an entry that has run or will not; an upstream state that moved; a file over its budget |

Apply three lenses, in order, and report what each found, including nothing:

1. **Duplication**: one finding stated in two places where one home should hold it.
2. **Staleness**: would the campaign still write this today? Grep for "not yet built", "not yet run",
   "blocked on", "expected shortly", "being lifted", "build under test", and check register entries
   whose dependency has been discharged. A discharged caveat misleads as much as a missing one.
3. **Weight**: does it change what a reader concludes or does? A caveat naming no discharging
   measurement, or a result tied to no decision, goes on the list. Open questions, limits and
   negative results are kept unless the pass shows they carry nothing; when in doubt, keep and report.

A pass normally leaves its group shorter. Report the net word change. The `writing-standards` cutting
constraints bind it absolutely.
